/* Ad055 - Stack overflow when meshing TBB pool from STEP import
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Catalog section : §12.11 adversarial (sub-class: stack-overflow / resource-exhaustion)
   Sources         : 18-other-issues.md I064 (OCCT #688);
                     20-general-forums.md J020 (huge-faces-per-shell SO)
   See also        : Ad032
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   WARNING: This file is INTENTIONALLY MALFORMED (oversized topology)
   for parser-robustness testing. Do NOT use as exchange data.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Defect
     Recursive traversal of CLOSED_SHELL with O(10^5) faces overflows
     C-stack on Windows defaults; BRepMesh_IncrementalMesh with TBB
     stack-overflows under 1 MB stack default per thread.
   Reproducer recipe (scaled-down to ~80 faces; production: 10^5)
     One CLOSED_SHELL referencing many ADVANCED_FACEs that share a
     trivial degenerate boundary, sized so that recursive shell
     traversal exceeds Windows' default 1 MB thread stack.
   Expected kernel behavior
     Iterative traversal; configurable per-thread stack; or fall back
     to single-thread on overflow; emit E_STACK_BUDGET.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*/
